      'Life-cycle key: Part A — s1, s2, s9 concept; s3, s4 development; s5 production; s6 utilization; s7 support; s8 retirement. Part B — g1 continue; g2 begin; g3 go to/restart (preferred, after R06a p.381’s “were restarted”; “begin another stage or stages” also accepted, R06b p.385); g4 pause; g5 terminate. Part C — r1 schedule; r2 event; r3 evidence. Written prompts: Part B answers should name an observable that would flip the decision (e.g. g1: both open concerns closed with signed positions); Part C answers should name the type’s characteristic risk and a guard (e.g. r1: confirm entry criteria before the date).',
      'Conflict-matrix key (nine stakeholders: STK-001, 003, 004, 005, 006, 007, 008, 010, 013; five variables): 28 conflicts (V1 6, V2 12, V3 2, V4 2, V5 6). Two tie at weight 25: V2 STK-003 vs STK-007 and V5 STK-003 vs STK-013; six at 20. Structural pair STK-003 ↔ STK-004 on V1, V2, V4, V5 (total 80), then STK-004 ↔ STK-005 (48), STK-001 ↔ STK-004 (36) and STK-003 ↔ STK-008 (30). Sensitivity: with Communities’ influence at 3 the top pair still leads (60 vs 36); at 2 it still leads (40 vs 30).',
      'L2 model answer and the reference baseline: the reference map STK-001..014 (14 stakeholders in 8 categories, covering all six S04 classes) with REL-001..008 (including REL-002 conflicts-with) meets the stakeholder, category, rating and relationship checks, and the reference concerns CON-001..016 meet “≥ 1 CON per STK”: every stakeholder has a concern of its own (test-asserted). Two of them were added after the independent review found the gap (W2-F04), which is itself a teaching point: CON-015 (fleet delivery and certification progress) for the OEM, STK-011, which had no concern; and CON-016 (land use and zoning of vertiport sites) for the City planning authority, STK-013, which had only shared the residents’ noise concern CON-012 — a shared concern whose text belongs to another stakeholder is not that stakeholder’s concern. Reference AROU v0, all linked by “affects” to concerns: A-001 passenger wait tolerance is 15 min (FICTIONAL); A-002 turnaround charging concentrated at 3 hub vertiports; A-007 a turnaround charger is occupied 20 min per turnaround (the course-wide convention: the 25 min hub turnaround is 5 min of pad work (rotor stop, safety check, charger connection) plus 20 min of charging, with boarding overlapping the charge; with two pads per turnaround charger, each charger is busy only for the 20 min charge, so 48 charges per charger per 16 h day; FICTIONAL); R-001 charging capacity lags fleet growth (condition–if–then form); O-001 integrated public-transport ticketing; U-001 aircraft weather limits not yet published. A further example in the same form, under the next free risk ID: R-009 (proposed; not in the reference) “Given that two of the six planned sites are in residential districts (FICTIONAL), if the City planning authority refuses them, then the demand catchment shrinks and the fleet plan is oversized”, affecting STK-013.',
